NAME
    cophist - coprocessor register history

SYNOPSIS
    cophist [<reg>] [<count>]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the retained history of the cartridge coprocessor's registers -
    the SuperFX GSU, the SA-1, or a NEC DSP - one row per refresh, oldest
    first. Where `regs` shows the instant, this shows the run-up to it.

    Give <reg> to follow a single register (SFR, PBR, R15, ...) instead of
    the whole file, and <count> to change how many rows are shown from the
    default 16. The header also reports how many refreshes the registers
    have gone unchanged, which is the direct answer to "when did the chip
    stop".

    Prints nothing useful on a cartridge with no coprocessor, which is most
    of them.

EXAMPLES
    cophist
    cophist SFR 64
    cophist R15
